      "side": 1,
      "message": "ubernit: put fUseColorXform after the std::optionals. This will have no impact now, but if we add more booleans or 4-byte types, this struct will be able to have less padding. In other words\n\n```\nstruct/class {\n  bool alpha;\n  std::optional\u003c\u003e beta;\n  bool gamma;\n}\n```\ntakes up more space than\n```\nstruct/class {\n  std::optional\u003c\u003e beta;\n  bool gamma;\n  bool alpha;\n}\n```\nor \n```\nstruct/class {\n  bool gamma;\n  bool alpha;\n  std::optional\u003c\u003e beta;\n}\n```\nIt\u0027s good practice [citation needed] to put larger fields first and smaller fields later to encourage better packing.",
